  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Clients and employers pay for judgment, reliability and the ability to solve problems quickly. They judge you by clear examples and by how well you understand current tools and norms.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing your offer in two sentences that a stranger can understand.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and starting a new career after 50 and 60: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools help with drafting, research and scheduling. They lower the cost of starting a small practice.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, trust and relationships hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and learn; later, own client work and decisions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="better">Alternatives that can beat a general starting a new career after 50 and 60 path</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Alternative</th>
          <th>Why it can beat it</th>
          <th>Catch</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Alternative"><strong>Full retirement</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat it">Rest</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">No new income</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Alternative"><strong>Part-time employment</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat it">Steady involvement</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">Lower flexibility</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Alternative"><strong>Own practice</strong></td>
